    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d221">

                <pb facs="0297" n="1031" xml:id="pg1031"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Baker to Mr. Gresham.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">San
                                Jose Costa Rica</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1895-04-24"><hi rendition="#italic">April 24, 1895</hi></date>.
                        (Received May 2.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 506.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have just received from the Government of
                    Nicaragua the inclosed telegraphic message in regard to the trouble of that
                    Government with Great Britain. I hand you both the original and the translation,
                    notwithstanding that Government has doubtless forwarded the same to you through
                    Minister Guzman. I simply acknowledged the receipt of the message by wire.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lewis Baker.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>




